    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0169" n="77" xml:id="pg77"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Harris.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 42, of the 21st ultimo, reporting your refusal to issue a passport
                    to Mrs. Elenora Eisenschimmel.</p>
                <p>The Department approves your action in the matter.</p>
                <p>Your remarks in reference to applicants for passports who fail to fulfill their
                    declared intention to return to the United States are very sensible and indicate
                    the proper course to be followed in such cases.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
